baseline.response:
Use `Isolate.run`. If the callback throws, the error is rethrown in the calling isolate. If the isolate dies without returning a result, the future completes with a `RemoteError` instead of waiting forever. Add a timeout and catch both cases in the UI state so it can't hang.

## Compression service

```dart
import 'dart:isolate';
import 'dart:typed_data';
import 'package:image/image.dart' as img;

class CompressionException implements Exception {
  CompressionException(this.message);
  final String message;
  @override
  String toString() => message;
}

/// Runs in a background isolate. `codec` is deliberately caller-controlled
/// so an invalid value can be used to trigger a failure.
Uint8List _compress(({Uint8List bytes, String codec, int quality}) args) {
  final decoded = img.decodeImage(args.bytes);
  if (decoded == null) {
    throw CompressionException('Could not decode image data');
  }
  switch (args.codec) {
    case 'jpg':
      return img.encodeJpg(decoded, quality: args.quality);
    case 'png':
      return img.encodePng(decoded);
    default:
      throw CompressionException('Unsupported codec: "${args.codec}"');
  }
}

Future<Uint8List> compressImage(
  Uint8List bytes, {
  String codec = 'jpg',
  int quality = 80,
  Duration timeout = const Duration(seconds: 30),
}) {
  return Isolate.run(
    () => _compress((bytes: bytes, codec: codec, quality: quality)),
  ).timeout(timeout); // guards against a stuck or never-returning isolate
}
```

## UI state that always resolves

```dart
import 'package:flutter/material.dart';

sealed class CompressState {}
class Idle extends CompressState {}
class Loading extends CompressState {}
class Done extends CompressState { Done(this.bytes); final Uint8List bytes; }
class Failed extends CompressState { Failed(this.message); final String message; }

class CompressPage extends StatefulWidget {
  const CompressPage({super.key, required this.input});
  final Uint8List input;
  @override
  State<CompressPage> createState() => _CompressPageState();
}

class _CompressPageState extends State<CompressPage> {
  CompressState _state = Idle();

  Future<void> _run(String codec) async {
    setState(() => _state = Loading());
    try {
      final out = await compressImage(widget.input, codec: codec);
      if (!mounted) return;
      setState(() => _state = Done(out));
    } on TimeoutException {
      if (!mounted) return;
      setState(() => _state = Failed('Compression timed out'));
    } on CompressionException catch (e) {
      if (!mounted) return;
      setState(() => _state = Failed(e.message));
    } catch (e) {
      // RemoteError, isolate crash, OOM, etc.
      if (!mounted) return;
      setState(() => _state = Failed('Compression failed: $e'));
    }
  }

  @override
  Widget build(BuildContext context) {
    return Scaffold(
      body: Center(
        child: switch (_state) {
          Idle() => Column(mainAxisSize: MainAxisSize.min, children: [
              ElevatedButton(onPressed: () => _run('jpg'), child: const Text('Compress (valid)')),
              ElevatedButton(onPressed: () => _run('bogus'), child: const Text('Compress (invalid codec)')),
            ]),
          Loading() => const CircularProgressIndicator(),
          Done(:final bytes) => Text('Compressed to ${bytes.length} bytes'),
          Failed(:final message) => Column(mainAxisSize: MainAxisSize.min, children: [
              Text(message, style: const TextStyle(color: Colors.red)),
              TextButton(onPressed: () => setState(() => _state = Idle()), child: const Text('Retry')),
            ]),
        },
      ),
    );
  }
}
```

(Add `import 'dart:async';` for `TimeoutException`.)

## Test that the failure surfaces

```dart
test('invalid codec throws instead of hanging', () async {
  final bytes = Uint8List.fromList(img.encodePng(img.Image(width: 8, height: 8)));
  expect(
    compressImage(bytes, codec: 'bogus', timeout: const Duration(seconds: 5)),
    throwsA(isA<CompressionException>()),
  );
});
```

## Notes

- **Why it doesn't hang:** every path ends in a state change. Success goes to `Done`, a thrown exception or isolate death goes to `Failed`, and a stall goes to `Failed` via the timeout. `Loading` is never a resting state.
- **Timeout caveat:** `.timeout` only stops waiting. It does not kill the isolate. If you need cancellation, use `Isolate.spawn` with `onError`/`onExit` ports and call `isolate.kill(priority: Isolate.immediate)` on timeout.
- **Exceptions across isolates:** a custom exception must only hold sendable fields (such as a `String`), as above. If it can't be sent, you get a `RemoteError` with the stringified message, which the generic `catch` already covers.
- **Web:** `Isolate.run` isn't supported on Flutter web, so use `compute` or a web worker there.

